From: damnbitimcrit <333091414+damnbitimcrit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [D3D12] Replay and execute submissions on a submission thread

Replaying the deferred command list into the Direct3D 12 command list,
closing and executing it took 2.8 ms of the GPU command processor
thread's 7 ms per frame in a busy Halo 3 scene (gpu_thread_profile),
46% of its time.

With d3d12_submission_thread (default on, read at every submission),
EndSubmission hands the recorded commands (swapped in O(1) into one of
two job slots), the command allocator and the submission number to a
"GPU Submission" thread. That thread resets the allocator and the
command list, replays, closes and executes it, then signals the
submission fence with that number. The GPU thread reserves the number
at the hand-off, so every recorded tag, allocator reuse and fence-gated
release stays as before: a submission counts as completed only after
its fence value, signaled after its execution.

The GPU thread waits for the submission thread before anything that
must come after the submissions on the direct queue: at each swap
(before the presenter signals its refresher fence and publishes the
guest output image for painting on the same queue), before the
out-of-submission fence signal, UpdateTileMappings and PIX captures,
and when the setting is turned off. Two immediate releases of readback
buffers a pending submission may copy to are deferred to submission
completion.

The GPU profile reports the submissions handed off, the GPU thread's
waits for the submission thread (and those at the swaps), and where
replaying and executing ran; the Halo 3 GPU thread line adds the waits
and the submission thread's busy time.
